From dfed39bf9e5d2955b0b9a3ccfda54fbb617e5649 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:36:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][DRM] No commit of a request before that cannot show
 the frame

Issue #33: after a refused test of the change to a frame-packed mode,
Kodi committed the request it took last with the new frame in its
plane. The frame's buffer (2048x2205) was smaller than what that plane
shows (3840x2160 of a 2D mode), which the kernel refuses before
anything else (drm_framebuffer_check_src_coords(): "No space left on
device"): three error lines for each 3D video, the next mode taken all
the same.

Such a request is not made now (FALLBACK_FRAME::GoesOut(), the kernel's
own check): the screen keeps what it shows, and Kodi goes on as after a
refused commit, as the kernel would have answered, so the next mode is
taken as before. And a refused change to a frame-packed mode, which
Kodi follows with the 3D layout that comes next, is said as a warning
that says so; every other refused test is an error as before.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/CMakeLists.txt  |  1 +
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.cpp   | 79 ++++++++++++++++++++++----
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.h     |  5 +-
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/FallbackFrame.h | 77 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 150 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/FallbackFrame.h

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/CMakeLists.txt b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/CMakeLists.txt
